    "title": "Downtown Canandaigua to host 'St. Paddy's Sip & Stroll' this weekend - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kiley Wren ,\n11 hours ago\nCANANDAIGUA, N.Y. — Canandaigua’s “St. Paddy’s Sip & Stroll” returns this weekend!\nOn Saturday, people 21 and older will be able to sample beverages and bites at more than 25 locations in downtown Canandaigua.\nParticipants will get an all-access wristband and tasting passport, which will allow them to make stops at local wineries, breweries, restaurants, shops, and galleries.\nThe event goes from 3-6 p.m. Saturday. Tickets are available for $20 in advance and will include a keepsake tasting glass, access to all tasting locations, and entry into a gift certificate giveaway. If not sold out, tickets the day of the event will be $25.\nCheck-in will be at 111 South Main Street from 3-5 p.m. You must have a valid ID at check-in.\nTo learn more and get tickets, click here.\nMore St. Patrick’s Day events Besides the sip and stroll, there are so many more upcoming events in the Rochester area to celebrate Irish heritage ahead of St. Patrick’s Day, which falls on Tuesday, March 17.\nClick here to read about some of the events happening this year\nRELATED STORIES:",
